   "text": "location history   -   Cassandra",
   "originalText": "location history   -   Cassandra",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cql",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 600,
   "y": 416,
   "width": 520,
   "height": 160,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100057,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700399,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "cql_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "cql_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 608,
   "y": 427,
   "width": 504,
   "height": 137,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100058,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700406,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "CREATE TABLE location_history (\n    user_id  bigint,\n    bucket   int,        -- DAY NUMBER: bounds the partition\n    ts       timestamp,\n    lat      float,\n    lng      float,\n    accuracy_m smallint,\n    PRIMARY KEY ((user_id, bucket), ts)\n) WITH CLUSTERING ORDER BY (ts DESC)\n  AND compaction = {'class': 'TimeWindowCompaction...'};",
   "originalText": "CREATE TABLE location_history (\n    user_id  bigint,\n    bucket   int,        -- DAY NUMBER: bounds the partition\n    ts       timestamp,\n    lat      float,\n    lng      float,\n    accuracy_m smallint,\n    PRIMARY KEY ((user_id, bucket), ts)\n) WITH CLUSTERING ORDER BY (ts DESC)\n  AND compaction = {'class': 'TimeWindowCompaction...'};",
   "fontSize": 11,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "cql",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "c2a",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 600,
   "y": 592,
   "width": 413,
   "height": 96,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100059,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700413,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Why Cassandra, not the relational store: 333,000 appends/sec\nwith essentially no reads - the most write-skewed profile in\nthe design. LSM storage turns every write into a sequential\nmemtable append plus an eventual SSTable flush: no in-place\npage updates, no B-tree splits. A relational store at this\nrate would spend its life on random writes and index\nmaintenance for data nobody queries interactively.",
   "originalText": "Why Cassandra, not the relational store: 333,000 appends/sec\nwith essentially no reads - the most write-skewed profile in\nthe design. LSM storage turns every write into a sequential\nmemtable append plus an eventual SSTable flush: no in-place\npage updates, no B-tree splits. A relational store at this\nrate would spend its life on random writes and index\nmaintenance for data nobody queries interactively.",
   "fontSize": 11,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "c2b",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 600,
   "y": 724,
   "width": 413,
   "height": 123,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100060,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700420,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Why the partition key is (user_id, bucket) and not just\nuser_id: one active user contributes ~2,880 rows/day, so a\nyear is a million-row partition and several years no longer\nfits comfortably on one node. A Cassandra partition is the\nunit of storage AND of repair, so unbounded growth is a real\noperational problem. A day bucket bounds every partition BY\nCONSTRUCTION; the cost is that a multi-day query reads\nseveral partitions - fine, since history has no latency\nrequirement.",
   "originalText": "Why the partition key is (user_id, bucket) and not just\nuser_id: one active user contributes ~2,880 rows/day, so a\nyear is a million-row partition and several years no longer\nfits comfortably on one node. A Cassandra partition is the\nunit of storage AND of repair, so unbounded growth is a real\noperational problem. A day bucket bounds every partition BY\nCONSTRUCTION; the cost is that a multi-day query reads\nseveral partitions - fine, since history has no latency\nrequirement.",
   "fontSize": 11,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "c2c",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 600,
   "y": 890,
   "width": 413,
   "height": 96,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100061,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700427,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "ts DESC because history queries are 'recent first': the\nnewest rows are physically first, so a LIMIT query stops\nimmediately instead of reverse-scanning the partition.\n\nTimeWindowCompactionStrategy groups SSTables by time window,\nso expiring old data DROPS WHOLE FILES rather than rewriting\nthem - the same principle as the message queue's segments.",
   "originalText": "ts DESC because history queries are 'recent first': the\nnewest rows are physically first, so a LIMIT query stops\nimmediately instead of reverse-scanning the partition.\n\nTimeWindowCompactionStrategy groups SSTables by time window,\nso expiring old data DROPS WHOLE FILES rather than rewriting\nthem - the same principle as the message queue's segments.",
   "fontSize": 11,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "c2d",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 600,
   "y": 1014,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 68,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100062,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700434,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Kafka sits in front, partitioned by user_id, for two reasons:\nit decouples the WS server's latency from Cassandra's, so a\nCassandra hiccup cannot touch the live path; and it is a\nreplay buffer, so an outage causes a DELAY rather than a\npermanent gap.",
   "originalText": "Kafka sits in front, partitioned by user_id, for two reasons:\nit decouples the WS server's latency from Cassandra's, so a\nCassandra hiccup cannot touch the live path; and it is a\nreplay buffer, so an outage causes a DELAY rather than a\npermanent gap.",
   "fontSize": 11,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
