  {
   "id": "fr_n",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1170,
   "y": 680,
   "width": 249,
   "height": 30,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100087,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700609,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "stored BIDIRECTIONALLY: (A,B) and\n(B,A) are both inserted",
   "originalText": "stored BIDIRECTIONALLY: (A,B) and\n(B,A) are both inserted",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "c3a",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1170,
   "y": 722,
   "width": 426,
   "height": 192,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100088,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700616,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Why both directions. The one query this table exists to serve\nis friendsOf(user_id), run once per connection. One row per\npair would make it WHERE user_id = ? OR friend_id = ? - which\ncannot use a single index efficiently and, once sharded on\nuser_id, becomes a SCATTER-GATHER ACROSS EVERY SHARD to find\nrows where the user appears in the second column.\n\nDuplicating the row makes friendsOf a single-shard,\nsingle-index range scan, with PRIMARY KEY (user_id, friend_id)\nclustering all of one user's friends together. The cost is 2x\nstorage and the obligation to write both rows in one\ntransaction. Trading storage for the elimination of a\nscatter-gather on the connect path is straightforwardly\ncorrect.",
   "originalText": "Why both directions. The one query this table exists to serve\nis friendsOf(user_id), run once per connection. One row per\npair would make it WHERE user_id = ? OR friend_id = ? - which\ncannot use a single index efficiently and, once sharded on\nuser_id, becomes a SCATTER-GATHER ACROSS EVERY SHARD to find\nrows where the user appears in the second column.\n\nDuplicating the row makes friendsOf a single-shard,\nsingle-index range scan, with PRIMARY KEY (user_id, friend_id)\nclustering all of one user's friends together. The cost is 2x\nstorage and the obligation to write both rows in one\ntransaction. Trading storage for the elimination of a\nscatter-gather on the connect path is straightforwardly\ncorrect.",
   "fontSize": 11,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "c3b",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1170,
   "y": 936,
   "width": 413,
   "height": 68,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100089,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700623,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "sharing_enabled DEFAULT FALSE puts the opt-in in the SCHEMA\nrather than in application code: a bug in a settings screen\nmust not be able to turn on location sharing for someone who\nnever asked. Defaults are the cheapest place to encode a\nprivacy requirement.",
   "originalText": "sharing_enabled DEFAULT FALSE puts the opt-in in the SCHEMA\nrather than in application code: a bug in a settings screen\nmust not be able to turn on location sharing for someone who\nnever asked. Defaults are the cheapest place to encode a\nprivacy requirement.",
   "fontSize": 11,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "c3c",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1170,
   "y": 1016,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 55,
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100090,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700630,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "This store must be sized for the RECONNECT STORM, not for\nsteady state: read rate is driven by connection churn, so\nsteady state is near-zero and a mass reconnect is briefly 10M\nreads. An unusual sizing criterion, driven by a failure mode.",
   "originalText": "This store must be sized for the RECONNECT STORM, not for\nsteady state: read rate is driven by connection churn, so\nsteady state is near-zero and a mass reconnect is briefly 10M\nreads. An unusual sizing criterion, driven by a failure mode.",
   "fontSize": 11,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d3",
   "type": "line",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1096,
   "width": 1680,
   "height": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#cbd5e1",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
