  },
  {
   "id": "dl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1288,
   "width": 710,
   "height": 21,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100095,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700665,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Where the guarantees go - and note that they run OPPOSITE to volume",
   "originalText": "Where the guarantees go - and note that they run OPPOSITE to volume",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1322,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 227,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100096,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700672,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "live location            EVENTUAL, last-write-wins, bounded by TTL   each key has exactly ONE writer - the server holding\n                                                                    that connection - so there is no write conflict to\n                                                                    resolve. A 30-second-stale read is the product, not a\n                                                                    compromise.\nlocation fan-out         AT-MOST-ONCE, unordered                    ordering is resolved at the RECEIVER by timestamp;\n                                                                    an ordered transport would cost far more than it is worth\nlocation history         EVENTUAL, at-least-once                    a duplicate row with the same (user_id, bucket, ts) key\n                                                                    is an idempotent overwrite in Cassandra - duplication is\n                                                                    harmless BY CONSTRUCTION, so exactly-once is wasted effort\nfriendships              STRONG, read-your-writes                   a new friend not immediately visible never gets\n                                                                    subscribed, and silently does not appear\nsharing_enabled / radius  STRONG                                     turning sharing OFF must take effect immediately and must\n                                                                    never be read from a lagging replica - the failure mode is\n                                                                    leaking a location the user just asked to stop sharing",
   "originalText": "live location            EVENTUAL, last-write-wins, bounded by TTL   each key has exactly ONE writer - the server holding\n                                                                    that connection - so there is no write conflict to\n                                                                    resolve. A 30-second-stale read is the product, not a\n                                                                    compromise.\nlocation fan-out         AT-MOST-ONCE, unordered                    ordering is resolved at the RECEIVER by timestamp;\n                                                                    an ordered transport would cost far more than it is worth\nlocation history         EVENTUAL, at-least-once                    a duplicate row with the same (user_id, bucket, ts) key\n                                                                    is an idempotent overwrite in Cassandra - duplication is\n                                                                    harmless BY CONSTRUCTION, so exactly-once is wasted effort\nfriendships              STRONG, read-your-writes                   a new friend not immediately visible never gets\n                                                                    subscribed, and silently does not appear\nsharing_enabled / radius  STRONG                                     turning sharing OFF must take effect immediately and must\n                                                                    never be read from a lagging replica - the failure mode is\n                                                                    leaking a location the user just asked to stop sharing",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1602,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100097,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700679,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The asymmetry worth naming: the WEAKEST guarantees apply to the highest-volume data (positions, 333k/sec) and the STRONGEST\nto the lowest-volume data (privacy settings, a handful per second). That is the correct arrangement, and it is the inverse of\nwhat a uniform 'we use a strongly consistent database' approach produces - which spends the strong-consistency budget on the\ndata that needs it least.",
   "originalText": "The asymmetry worth naming: the WEAKEST guarantees apply to the highest-volume data (positions, 333k/sec) and the STRONGEST\nto the lowest-volume data (privacy settings, a handful per second). That is the correct arrangement, and it is the inverse of\nwhat a uniform 'we use a strongly consistent database' approach produces - which spends the strong-consistency budget on the\ndata that needs it least.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d5",
   "type": "line",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1692,
   "width": 1680,
   "height": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#cbd5e1",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
